  <title>Verbosity</title>
  <p>
    Configure how much object information is displayed in braille.
  </p>
  <section id="settings-verbosity">
    <title>Settings</title>
    <p>
      <em style="strong">Preferences location:</em>
      <gui>Braille</gui> category, <gui>Verbosity</gui> group.
    </p>
    <p>
      <em style="strong">Available settings:</em>
    </p>
    <list>
      <item>
        <p>
          <gui>Object presentation is detailed</gui>: Controls whether
          Orca shows more detailed object information. Default: on.
        </p>
      </item>
      <item>
        <p>
          <gui>Show context (ancestors)</gui>: Controls whether
          Orca shows contextual information about the current object, such as the panel it is
          inside. Default: on.
        </p>
      </item>
      <item>
        <p>
          <gui>Abbreviated role names</gui>: Controls whether
          Orca uses abbreviated role names, such as btn for button. Default: off.
        </p>
      </item>
      <item>
        <p>
          <gui>Mnemonics</gui>: Controls whether Orca
          shows shortcut letters, such as the F used with Alt to open a File menu, in braille.
          Default: on.
        </p>
      </item>
    </list>
  </section>
